ck the lead with G8, and the 16k gave it straight back with G7. After that White's lead never fell below 13 points.", "moments": [{"turn": 15, "text": "The 16k's G4 moved Black's lead from -5.2 to -14.0, a loss of 8.8 points. The engine preferred G6. It was the first big swing toward White."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "Opus 5.5's H3 moved Black's lead from -10.6 to +3.9, a 14.5-point loss, after J4 had already lost 11.7. The engine wanted C6 both times. Opus 5.5 had been well ahead and gave the lead away here."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "The 16k's C7 took Black's lead from -12.9 to -31.2, losing 18.3 points. The engine's choice was E6. The stones around C7, C8 and D8 sit at the edge of a position where White's centre was still alive."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "Opus 5.5's G8 was the worst move of its game, 40.6 points lost, and Black's lead went from -34.1 to +6.5. The engine's choice was E6, the empty point in the middle of the board. Opus 5.5 had been about 34 points ahead and gave it all back."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "The 16k answered with G7, the worst move of the game at 44.7 points. The lead went from +6.5 back to -38.2, and the engine again wanted E6. Neither side took that point, and the swings alone were worth about 85 points."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "Opus 5.5 finally played E6, the engine's first choice, and lost nothing (-0.2). Black stood at -45.2 afterwards. From here the game was a mop-up that ended in two passes, and White finished with 13 captures."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and reports groups and their liberties, count.py only does an area count of the current position, and the games.md append is note-keeping; none of them choose, rank or look ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}